# [INTAREA](../wg/intarea.html)

## Summary

The INTAREA working group met during IETF 127. The session included working group document status updates, discussions on legacy registry cleanups, updating the IP tunnels architecture document, Internet checksum updates, ICMP extensions and acceptable use policies, chartering a new DNS protocol working group, and signaling mechanisms for IP enclave boundaries. 

The session marked a chair transition: Wassim Haddad is stepping down after ten years of service as INTAREA co-chair, and Tim Winter will be joining Carlos Jesús Bernardos as co-chair.

---

## Key Discussion Points

### Administration and WG Status
- **Chairs' Introduction**: Presented via [Chairs' slides](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-intarea-1-chairs-slides-03).
- **Leadership Transition**: The WG thanked Wassim Haddad for his ten years of service as INTAREA co-chair. Tim Winter will assume the co-chair role alongside Carlos Jesús Bernardos.
- **Document Status Updates**:
  - `draft-ietf-intarea-proxy-config` is in the RFC Editor queue (AUTH48 state).
