### Presentation: Extending ICMP for Interface and Next-Hop Identification
- **Presenter**: Soren
- **Slides**: [Extending ICMP for Interface and Next-hop Identification](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-intarea-5-extending-icmp-for-interface-and-next-hop-identification-00)
- **Discussion**:
  - Revises RFC 5837 to allow routers to report sub-IP/physical link components (e.g., egress LAG legs) using a newly assigned IANA Class 7 ICMP extension object.
  - Jen Linkova expressed concern regarding amplification attacks and recommended that extensions be disabled by default and restricted via access control lists.
  - Bill Fenner noted that RFC 5837 currently cannot represent IPv6 next hops for IPv4 routes and suggested resolving this issue in the update, as well as considering experimental codepoint handling under RFC 3692.

