### Presentation: Proposed New DNS Protocol WG: Charter Discussion
- **Presenter**: Jim Reid
- **Slides**: [Proposed new DNS protocol WG: charter discussion (follow-up from DNSOP)](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-intarea-6-proposed-new-dns-protocol-wg-charter-discussion-follow-up-from-dnsop-01)
- **Discussion**:
  - Proposal to split DNSOP by keeping operational topics in DNSOP (OPS area) and creating a new DNS protocol maintenance working group in the INT area.
  - Feedback focused on simplifying the proposed charter text. Jen Linkova and Jim Reid agreed to remove confusing language regarding scope limits ("DNS version 2").
  - Éric Vyncke confirmed that the INT Area ADs will initiate community last call and IESG evaluation for chartering the new WG.
  - Bob Hinden questioned specific IANA registry wording in the charter; Jim Reid noted that keeping the charter text concise is preferable.

