### Presentation: IP Enclave Boundary Signaling
- **Presenter**: Eric Kline
- **Slides**: [IP Enclave Boundary Signaling](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-intarea-8-ip-enclave-boundary-signaling-00)
- **Discussion**:
  - Proposes RFC 4884 ICMP extension objects attached to unreachable or admin-prohibited messages to signal link metrics (e.g., expected time to link usability, expected link delay, denied by link policy) for intermittent connectivity across administrative boundaries, working alongside Provisioning Domains (PvDs).
  - Applicable to deep space/planetary networks, terrestrial multi-homing source address validation (Jen Linkova), and maritime satellite links (Bob Hinden).
  - Éric Vyncke pointed out related work in the SCHC (chic) working group regarding sleeping node signaling.
  - Multiple participants (Carsten Bormann, Dave Thaler, Éric Vyncke) noted in chat and at the mic that the term "enclave" is typically associated with secure enclaves, suggesting alternative terminology.

